('127.251.d.5.D',4,'A payday loan is risky because it usually has:','["Low fees", "Long terms", "No interest", "Very high fees and short repayment terms"]'::jsonb,3,'Payday loans trap borrowers.','original'),
('127.251.d.5.E',3,'A bank considers a borrower''s income, credit history, and:','["Existing debts", "Hobbies", "Favorite color", "Shoe size"]'::jsonb,0,'Lenders assess repayment ability.','original'),
('127.251.d.5.E',4,'A loan application package often includes:','["A recipe", "Proof of income and identification", "A map", "A poem"]'::jsonb,1,'Documents verify the borrower.','original'),
('127.251.d.5.F',3,'A scatterplot of months paid versus loan balance with equal monthly payments will generally show:','["No trend", "A circle", "A downward trend", "An upward trend"]'::jsonb,2,'Balance falls over time.','original'),
('127.251.d.5.F',4,'Using a scatterplot to predict the balance after 40 payments involves:','["Guessing", "Ignoring the data", "Using only the first point", "Fitting a trend and interpreting it"]'::jsonb,3,'Trends support prediction.','original'),
('127.251.d.5.G',3,'A higher credit score generally means a borrower is:','["A lower risk to lenders", "Banned from loans", "Unknown", "A higher risk"]'::jsonb,0,'High scores signal reliability.','original'),
('127.251.d.5.G',4,'Which factor typically has the largest effect on a credit score?','["Address", "Payment history", "Phone brand", "Hair color"]'::jsonb,1,'On-time payments matter most.','original'),
('127.251.d.5.H',3,'A negative credit report can lead to:','["Bonus points", "Guaranteed loans", "Higher interest rates or denied credit", "Lower rates"]'::jsonb,2,'Poor credit costs more.','original'),
('127.251.d.5.H',4,'A negative report may also affect a consumer''s ability to:','["Vote", "Drive", "Pay no taxes", "Rent an apartment or get some jobs"]'::jsonb,3,'Credit checks are used widely.','original'),
('127.251.d.5.I',3,'Consumers are entitled to a free credit report from each major bureau:','["Once every 12 months at the official site", "Never", "Only if denied", "Every day"]'::jsonb,0,'AnnualCreditReport.com is the official source.','original'),
('127.251.d.5.I',4,'When reviewing a credit report, you should look for:','["The weather", "Accounts you do not recognize", "Sports scores", "Your favorite store"]'::jsonb,1,'Unknown accounts may be fraud.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.A',3,'Paying extra toward the principal on a mortgage usually:','["Extends the loan", "Raises interest", "Reduces total interest and shortens the loan", "Cancels the loan"]'::jsonb,2,'Extra principal saves interest.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.A',4,'Adding $100 per month to the principal payment affects the loan by:','["Raising the rate", "Increasing fees", "Doing nothing", "Lowering the balance faster than scheduled"]'::jsonb,3,'More principal reduces balance.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.B',3,'An amortization table shows each payment split between:','["Principal and interest", "Cash and checks", "Taxes and rent", "Wages and tips"]'::jsonb,0,'Payments cover both.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.B',4,'A $200,000 loan at 6% annual interest has a first-month interest of:','["$12,000", "$1,000", "$10,000", "$100"]'::jsonb,1,'200,000 x 0.005 = 1,000.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.C',3,'A 20% down payment on a $250,000 home is:','["$20,000", "$5,000", "$50,000", "$25,000"]'::jsonb,2,'0.20 x 250,000 = 50,000.','original'),
