('127.251.d.6.E',3,'Mortgage interest can be a tax deduction only if the taxpayer:','["Files no return", "Rents", "Itemizes deductions", "Takes the standard deduction"]'::jsonb,2,'Itemizing is needed.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.E',4,'If a taxpayer in the 22% bracket deducts $10,000 of mortgage interest and itemizes beyond the standard deduction, the tax savings are roughly:','["$22,000", "$220", "$10,000", "$2,200"]'::jsonb,3,'0.22 x 10,000 = 2,200.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.F',3,'Beyond the mortgage payment, homeowners pay for maintenance, insurance, and:','["Repairs and utilities", "Subscriptions only", "Rent", "Tuition"]'::jsonb,0,'Ownership adds costs.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.F',4,'A common guideline is to budget about 1% of a home''s value yearly for:','["Furniture", "Maintenance and repairs", "Streaming", "Vacations"]'::jsonb,1,'Upkeep is ongoing.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.G',3,'To keep paying a $1,200 mortgage after losing a job for 6 months, a homeowner would need to have saved about:','["$720", "$6,000", "$7,200", "$1,200"]'::jsonb,2,'6 x 1,200 = 7,200.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.G',4,'An emergency fund helps homeowners because it:','["Increases debt", "Raises the interest rate", "Lowers property value", "Covers payments during income loss"]'::jsonb,3,'Savings protect the home.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.H',3,'If a homeowner stops making mortgage payments, the lender may begin:','["Foreclosure", "A refund", "A raise", "A tax credit"]'::jsonb,0,'Foreclosure lets lenders recover the property.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.H',4,'A foreclosure typically harms a borrower''s:','["Hair", "Credit score for years", "Driving record", "School grades"]'::jsonb,1,'It stays on credit reports.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.I',3,'One advantage of renting over buying is:','["Building equity", "Tax deductions", "Less responsibility for major repairs", "Fixed payments forever"]'::jsonb,2,'Landlords handle repairs.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.I',4,'One advantage of buying over renting is:','["No risk", "No taxes", "No upkeep", "Building equity as the loan is paid"]'::jsonb,3,'Owners build equity.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.J',3,'The Multiple Listing Service lets users:','["Search and compare properties for sale", "File taxes", "Buy stocks", "Pay rent"]'::jsonb,0,'MLS lists homes.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.J',4,'Comparing price per square foot across listings helps buyers:','["Order furniture", "Judge value between homes", "Set taxes", "Pick a lender"]'::jsonb,1,'Unit price allows comparison.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.K',3,'A security deposit on an apartment is usually:','["Utilities", "A fee never returned", "Money held by the landlord and returned if there is no damage", "Monthly rent"]'::jsonb,2,'Deposits cover damage.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.K',4,'Before signing a lease, a renter should read the terms about:','["Neighbors'' cars", "The landlord''s hobbies", "Paint colors only", "Rent, length, and penalties for breaking the lease"]'::jsonb,3,'Know your obligations.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.L',3,'Renter''s insurance generally covers a tenant''s:','["Personal belongings and liability", "The landlord''s debts", "Property taxes", "The building structure"]'::jsonb,0,'The landlord insures the building.','original'),
('127.251.d.6.L',4,'When comparing renter''s insurance, you should check the premium and the:','["Logo", "Coverage limits and deductible", "Agent''s age", "Company color"]'::jsonb,1,'Coverage and cost both matter.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.A',3,'A $20,000 car loan at 0% interest for 60 months has a monthly payment of about:','["$500", "$1,000", "$333", "$200"]'::jsonb,2,'20,000 / 60 = 333.33.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.A',4,'An amortization table for a car loan shows how interest:','["Increases forever", "Stays the same", "Vanishes at the start", "Decreases as the balance falls"]'::jsonb,3,'Interest is based on the remaining balance.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.B',3,'Costs of owning a vehicle include fuel, insurance, repairs, and:','["Maintenance", "Tuition", "Rent", "Tips"]'::jsonb,0,'Upkeep is a recurring cost.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.B',4,'A driver spends $120 monthly on fuel, $90 on insurance, and $40 on maintenance. Monthly running costs are:','["$210", "$250", "$130", "$330"]'::jsonb,1,'120 + 90 + 40 = 250.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.C',3,'A lease usually has lower monthly payments than a loan but:','["The driver owns the car", "There are no mileage limits", "The driver does not build ownership", "No fees apply"]'::jsonb,2,'Leases have no equity.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.C',4,'Buying a car for $24,000 and keeping it 10 years, versus leasing repeatedly, is often cheaper because:','["Leases are free", "Taxes vanish", "Fuel costs vanish", "Ownership continues after the loan ends"]'::jsonb,3,'Long-term ownership spreads cost.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.D',3,'Two cars cost $18,000 and $22,000 to buy. Insurance and fuel are the same. The lower total cost depends on purchase price and:','["Maintenance and resale value", "Paint", "Mirrors", "Radio"]'::jsonb,0,'Total cost includes upkeep and resale.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.D',4,'To compare vehicles fairly, a buyer should calculate:','["Only the brand", "Total cost of ownership over several years", "Only the color", "Only the sticker price"]'::jsonb,1,'Look at the full cost.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.E',3,'A maintenance contract is useful when it:','["Raises repair costs", "Voids warranties", "Covers repairs the owner would otherwise pay", "Adds taxes"]'::jsonb,2,'Contracts shift risk.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.E',4,'Before buying an extended warranty, a consumer should compare its cost to:','["The dealer''s age", "The radio brand", "The car''s color", "Likely repair costs"]'::jsonb,3,'Value depends on expected repairs.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.F',3,'To keep a $400 car payment going for 3 months of lost income, a driver needs to have saved:','["$1,200", "$400", "$800", "$4,000"]'::jsonb,0,'3 x 400 = 1,200.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.F',4,'If a car payment cannot be made, the lender may:','["Forgive the loan", "Repossess the vehicle", "Wash the car", "Raise your income"]'::jsonb,1,'Secured loans allow repossession.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.G',3,'A driver''s education course may benefit a teen by:','["Eliminating tickets", "Voiding insurance", "Possibly lowering insurance premiums", "Raising premiums"]'::jsonb,2,'Insurers reward training.','original'),
('127.251.d.7.G',4,'When comparing driver education options, a student should compare:','["Car colors", "Slogans", "Logos", "Cost, schedule, and state approval"]'::jsonb,3,'Approved courses meet state rules.','original'),
('127.251.d.8.A',3,'Buying shares of stock through a broker is done in:','["The stock market", "A bank vault", "A pawn shop", "A post office"]'::jsonb,0,'Brokers trade securities.','original'),
('127.251.d.8.A',4,'A market order to buy a stock is executed:','["At a price you set", "At the best available current price", "Only next year", "Never"]'::jsonb,1,'Market orders fill at the current price.','original'),
('127.251.d.8.B',3,'A bond with $1,000 face value and 5% coupon pays annual interest of:','["$100", "$500", "$50", "$5"]'::jsonb,2,'0.05 x 1,000 = 50.','original'),
('127.251.d.8.B',4,'When market interest rates rise, existing bond prices generally:','["Rise", "Double", "Stay fixed", "Fall"]'::jsonb,3,'Prices move inversely to rates.','original'),
('127.251.d.8.C',3,'Which investment typically offers the highest risk and highest potential return?','["Stocks", "CDs", "Savings accounts", "Government bonds"]'::jsonb,0,'Stocks are volatile.','original'),
('127.251.d.8.C',4,'A mutual fund differs from a single stock because it:','["Holds only one company", "Pools many investors'' money into a diversified portfolio", "Has no risk", "Guarantees returns"]'::jsonb,1,'Funds offer diversification.','original'),
('127.251.d.8.D',3,'A diversified portfolio holds:','["One bond", "Only cash", "Many different investments", "One stock"]'::jsonb,2,'Diversification spreads risk.','original'),
('127.251.d.8.D',4,'Compared with a non-diversified portfolio, a diversified one generally has:','["Guaranteed returns", "Higher risk", "No fees", "Lower risk for similar returns"]'::jsonb,3,'Diversification reduces volatility.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.A',3,'Insurance that covers a set number of years and has no cash value is:','["Term life insurance", "Whole life insurance", "Renter''s insurance", "Auto insurance"]'::jsonb,0,'Term coverage expires.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.A',4,'A permanent policy differs from term in that it:','["Expires quickly", "Builds cash value and lasts for life", "Costs nothing", "Has no premiums"]'::jsonb,1,'Whole life accumulates value.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.B',3,'Using a needs approach, family income of $50,000 and a 10-times-income guideline suggest coverage of:','["$50,000", "$5,000,000", "$500,000", "$100,000"]'::jsonb,2,'10 x 50,000 = 500,000.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.B',4,'A needs approach to life insurance adds up debts, income replacement, and:','["Past purchases", "Vacations only", "Hobbies", "Future expenses such as education"]'::jsonb,3,'It estimates family needs.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.C',3,'Health insurance costs include premiums, deductibles, and:','["Copays", "Rent", "Wages", "Interest"]'::jsonb,0,'Out-of-pocket costs vary.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.C',4,'A plan with a $200 monthly premium costs how much per year in premiums?','["$240", "$2,400", "$200", "$1,200"]'::jsonb,1,'200 x 12 = 2,400.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.D',3,'Disability income insurance replaces part of income if a worker:','["Quits", "Is on vacation", "Cannot work due to illness or injury", "Gets a raise"]'::jsonb,2,'It protects earnings.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.D',4,'Many workers need disability insurance because their largest asset is often:','["Their car", "Their phone", "Their furniture", "Their ability to earn income"]'::jsonb,3,'Income is the key asset.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.E',3,'An umbrella policy gives extra:','["Liability coverage beyond other policies", "Pay raises", "Rain protection", "Life coverage"]'::jsonb,0,'It extends liability limits.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.E',4,'Before buying special coverage, a consumer should compare its benefit to its:','["Color", "Cost", "Age", "Name"]'::jsonb,1,'Weigh benefit against price.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.F',3,'Insurers set premiums using the process of:','["Coin tosses", "Rumor", "Actuarial analysis of risk", "Random guessing"]'::jsonb,2,'Actuaries use data.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.F',4,'Younger drivers often pay higher auto premiums because statistics show:','["Lower rates of accidents", "Better savings", "Longer commutes always", "Higher rates of accidents"]'::jsonb,3,'Risk drives price.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.G',3,'When selecting an insurance company, a buyer should check its:','["Financial strength rating and complaint record", "Slogan", "Building size", "Parking"]'::jsonb,0,'Ratings show reliability.','original'),
('127.251.d.9.G',4,'A good insurance agent should be:','["Unlicensed", "Licensed and able to explain options clearly", "Pushy", "Secretive"]'::jsonb,1,'Licensing and clarity matter.','original'),
('127.251.d.10.A',3,'A retirement plan offered by a nonprofit or school district is a:','["Roth IRA only", "Savings bond", "403(b)", "Checking account"]'::jsonb,2,'403(b)s serve public schools and nonprofits.','original'),
('127.251.d.10.A',4,'Qualified withdrawals from a Roth IRA in retirement are generally:','["Taxed twice", "Taxed at 100%", "Prohibited", "Tax-free"]'::jsonb,3,'Roth contributions are after-tax.','original'),
('127.251.d.10.B',3,'Starting to save for retirement earlier helps because of:','["Compounding over more years", "Lower contributions needed forever", "Fewer taxes", "Higher fees"]'::jsonb,0,'Time magnifies growth.','original')
